title:    Four tunnels, two gateways, both sessions up
subtitle: Two logical tunnels — and four tunnel resources, because each side declares its own
width:    940
---
$ gcloud compute vpn-tunnels list

NAME              REGION       STATUS       DETAILED_STATUS
branch-to-hub-t0  us-central1  ESTABLISHED  Tunnel is up and running.
branch-to-hub-t1  us-central1  ESTABLISHED  Tunnel is up and running.
hub-to-branch-t0  us-central1  ESTABLISHED  Tunnel is up and running.
hub-to-branch-t1  us-central1  ESTABLISHED  Tunnel is up and running.

$ gcloud compute vpn-gateways list

NAME       NETWORK
branch-gw  branch
hub-gw     hub

# FOUR tunnel resources for TWO logical tunnels, and this is what bills.
# Each side declares its own end, so $0.05/hour becomes $0.20/hour - the
# number to plan around is four, not two.
#
# Each gateway has two interfaces with their own public IPs, and the tunnels
# pair interface 0 to interface 0 and 1 to 1. Using only one interface carries
# NO availability SLA - not a reduced one. That is why there are two of
# everything here.
